k beyond the model API.\n\n**Most serious**\n1. **Isolation (`harness/src/clone-process.ts:52`):** on Node 24, which CI uses, the clone runs with no network restriction. In a test, a process under the same permission model was refused when it read a holdout fixture from disk, but got the same fixture over HTTP. A clone could therefore download the answers at verify time, for example from the public GitHub repository.\n2. **Secrets (11 dev fixtures, e.g. `dev-v5-cancel-at-mid-prorate.json:175`):** the hosted-invoice and PDF URLs carry a token that decodes to the real account ID, `acct_1UIrqUDSnaJHjCbZ`, plus an access secret. This undoes the scrubbing of the plain-text ID, and the secrets test does not catch it.\n3. **Integrity (`harness/src/fixtures.ts:138`):** the lock hashes `package.json` and `package-lock.json` but not the installed packages. I changed the Stripe SDK in the scratch copy and the lock check still passed.\n4. **Look counting (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:32`):** CI scores every holdout batch on every push and pull request, but its run-log line is thrown away. Those looks are missing from `runs.jsonl` and from the look counts in the reports.\n\n**Claims**\n5. **`GAPS.md:26`:** the \"a quarter of that batch is easy\" figures (74 errors, 343 substantive cases) are batch 2's, but they sit right after the batch 6 claim. On batch 6 itself, the 411 substantive cases give a bound of 1.11 % at 99 %, so \"below 1 % at 99 %\" does not hold for substantive changes there either. Neither `GAPS.md` nor the fidelity report says so.\n6. **`GAPS.md:84`:** it says LIF-03 and LIF-04 have no dev fixture and are unverified. `verify` reports LIF-03 verified (2 of 2) and LIF-04 failing (1 of 2).\n7. **`GAPS.md:60`:** it says the clone's 7 known failures are all outside the preview endpoint, but two of them fail on `create_preview`.\n\n**Clone and guard**\n8. **`clone/state.ts:246`:** objects not on a test clock are stamped with the real time, so one fixture's output changed between my run and the committed one. This breaks the determinism invariant; `verify` misses it because it checks only 10 dev fixtures.\n9. **`harness/hooks/guard-oracle.sh:106`:** the guard blocks the Write tool on the adapter and probe code, but lets shell commands rewrite them (`sed -i`, `cp`, `node -e`). The repository calls the guard a best-effort second line, so this one matters least.\n\nI found no evidence that the clone looks up recorded answers or special-cases probe inputs. The confidence bounds are computed correctly, and the sandbox copy keeps holdout files, seeds and git history out.","ttft_ms":2435,"type":"result","duration_ms":771159,"uuid":"e61d417f-1e06-48ac-8598-ad9169fc8ff8","ttft_stream_ms":2384,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":2384,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

